<onlyinclude>'''Simulated reality''' is the hypothesis or thought experiment that an experienced world may be generated by a computational or other simulation. It differs from ordinary virtual reality, where users know they are interacting with an engineered representation.

== Explanation ==
Philosophers investigate whether inhabitants of a sufficiently detailed simulation could distinguish it from a non-simulated world. Nick Bostrom's 2003 simulation argument explores conditional possibilities about future civilizations and simulations. The argument does not demonstrate that our world is simulated, and no generally accepted empirical evidence establishes that conclusion.

